# ARTICLE 12 — FINANCIAL COVENANTS AND REPORTING

**12.1 Minimum Debt Service Coverage Ratio.**

(a) Borrower shall maintain a DSCR of not less than 1.25 to 1.00 (the "**DSCR Covenant**"), tested as of the last day of each calendar quarter, commencing with the calendar quarter ending June 30, 2027 (being the first full calendar quarter ending after the twenty-fourth (24th) month following the Closing Date), and continuing quarterly thereafter. Each test shall be based on Net Operating Income for the trailing twelve (12) month period ending on the last day of the applicable calendar quarter and Annual Debt Service determined as of the last day of such quarter.

(b) Borrower shall deliver to Lender, concurrently with each quarterly test, a compliance certificate setting forth in reasonable detail the calculation of Net Operating Income, Annual Debt Service and DSCR, together with supporting operating statements and rent rolls.

(c) A failure to maintain the DSCR Covenant as of the end of any two (2) consecutive calendar quarters shall constitute an Event of Default in accordance with Section 14.1(i), subject to Borrower's right to cure in accordance with Section 12.6.

(d) Lender and Borrower acknowledge that the DSCR Covenant is measured against annual debt service calculated on a twenty-five (25) year amortization schedule and that the DSCR Covenant is not measured during the Interest-Only Period.

**12.2 Net Worth and Liquidity Covenants.**

(a) Borrower shall maintain at all times during the term of the Loan (i) a net worth of not less than One Million and No/100 Dollars ($1,000,000.00), and (ii) liquid assets (defined as cash, cash equivalents, marketable securities and unencumbered deposits held at federally insured depository institutions) of not less than Five Hundred Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($500,000.00).

(b) Guarantor shall maintain at all times during the term of the Loan (i) a net worth of not less than One Million and No/100 Dollars ($1,000,000.00), and (ii) liquid assets of not less than Five Hundred Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($500,000.00).

(c) Compliance with this Section 12.2 shall be tested annually, based on the financial statements and certificates delivered pursuant to Section 12.3.

**12.3 Financial Reporting.** Borrower shall deliver to Lender:

(a) Annual audited financial statements of Borrower, prepared in accordance with GAAP by an independent certified public accounting firm acceptable to Lender, within one hundred twenty (120) days after the end of Borrower's fiscal year;

(b) An annual personal financial statement of Guarantor, in form and detail reasonably satisfactory to Lender, within one hundred twenty (120) days after the end of each calendar year;

(c) Quarterly rent rolls for the Property, certified by Borrower as true, correct and complete, within thirty (30) days after the end of each calendar quarter;

(d) Annual property operating statements for the Property, including a detailed income and expense report and a comparison to the approved budget, within one hundred twenty (120) days after the end of Borrower's fiscal year;

(e) Copies of all Leases, lease amendments, lease guarantees and material lease correspondence executed or received by Borrower with respect to the Property, within ten (10) business days after execution or receipt; and

(f) Such other information regarding Borrower, Guarantor or the Property as Lender may reasonably request from time to time.

Borrower acknowledges that the Operating Agreement requires only annual financial statements "reviewed" (and not audited) by an independent certified public accountant, and that the reporting requirements of this Section 12.3 are more extensive than those in the Operating Agreement. Borrower shall cause the required audited financial statements to be prepared and delivered notwithstanding the Operating Agreement.

**12.4 Compliance Certificate.** Concurrently with the delivery of the annual financial statements and each quarterly rent roll, Borrower shall deliver to Lender a certificate of a manager or authorized officer of Borrower certifying that (a) the financial statements and rent rolls are true, correct and complete in all material respects, (b) no Event of Default exists or, if an Event of Default exists, specifying the nature and status thereof, and (c) Borrower is in compliance with Sections 12.1 and 12.2 (with the supporting calculations).

**12.5 Lender's Audit Rights.** Lender and its representatives may audit, examine and make copies of Borrower's books and records relating to the Property and the Renovation at any reasonable time upon reasonable prior notice, and may communicate directly with Borrower's accountants and, upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, with tenants. Borrower shall pay the reasonable costs of any such audit following an Event of Default.

**12.6 DSCR Cure.** Notwithstanding Section 14.1(i), Borrower may cure a failure to maintain the DSCR Covenant by paying to Lender, within thirty (30) days after Lender's written notice of such failure, an amount (the "**DSCR Cure Amount**") that, when applied to the outstanding principal balance of the Loan, would result in a DSCR of not less than 1.25 to 1.00 as of the end of the most recently ended calendar quarter, as reasonably determined by Lender and set forth in its notice. Any DSCR Cure Amount shall be applied to the outstanding principal balance of the Loan, shall not constitute a voluntary prepayment, shall not be subject to any prepayment premium, penalty or yield maintenance, and shall not relieve Borrower of the obligation to comply with the DSCR Covenant for any subsequent period. Borrower may exercise the cure right under this Section 12.6 not more than twice during the term of the Loan, and not more than once in any period of four (4) consecutive calendar quarters, and no cure shall be available with respect to any failure to maintain the DSCR Covenant occurring during the continuance of any other Event of Default.

**12.7 Guarantor Financial Statements; No Change in Guarantor.** Borrower shall cause Guarantor to deliver the financial statements and information required by Section 12.3(b), and Borrower shall promptly notify Lender of any change in the ownership or control of Guarantor or of Graydon Development Group LLC.

# ARTICLE 13 — PREPAYMENT

**13.1 Lockout Period.** The Loan may not be prepaid, in whole or in part, during the Lockout Period. No voluntary prepayment of principal shall be permitted during the Lockout Period. Any tender of payment in violation of this Section 13.1 is prohibited, and Lender may refuse to accept such tender. If Lender elects, in its sole discretion, to accept any such tender, the Yield Maintenance Premium shall be payable as though the prepayment had been made on the first day of the Yield Maintenance Period, in addition to all other amounts payable under the Loan Documents, and such acceptance shall not constitute a waiver of any Event of Default.

**13.2 Yield Maintenance Period.** From the expiration of the Lockout Period through the last day of the Yield Maintenance Period, the Loan may be prepaid in whole, but not in part, upon not less than thirty (30) days' prior written notice to Lender, and upon simultaneous payment of a yield maintenance premium (the "**Yield Maintenance Premium**") equal to the greater of:

(a) one percent (1.00%) of the outstanding principal balance of the Loan as of the date of prepayment; and

(b) the present value, discounted at the Treasury Rate, of the excess, if any, of (i) the interest that would have accrued on the principal amount being prepaid at the interest rate in effect under the Note on the date of prepayment (after giving effect to the SOFR Floor) for the period from the date of prepayment through the last day of the Yield Maintenance Period, over (ii) the interest that would accrue on such principal amount at a rate per annum equal to the Treasury Rate plus fifty (50) basis points (0.50%) for such period.

The present value described in clause (b) shall be calculated using monthly discounting, with each month's interest differential discounted from the last day of the applicable month to the date of prepayment, and shall in no event be less than zero. If the date of prepayment is not the first day of a month, the interest differential for the month in which the prepayment occurs shall be prorated on the basis of the actual number of days remaining in such month. The Yield Maintenance Premium shall be determined by Lender in good faith, and Lender's written calculation, absent manifest error, shall be conclusive and binding on Borrower.

**13.3 Open Prepayment Period.** During the final twelve (12) months of the term of the Loan (being from and after April 15, 2029 through the Maturity Date), the Loan may be prepaid in whole or in part, at any time and from time to time, without payment of any prepayment premium, penalty or yield maintenance amount, upon not less than fifteen (15) days' prior written notice to Lender.

**13.4 Notice; Conditions.** Each notice of prepayment shall be irrevocable and shall specify the proposed prepayment date and amount. No prepayment shall be effective unless and until (a) all accrued and unpaid interest, all late charges, all prepayment premiums or yield maintenance amounts due and all other Secured Obligations owing on the prepayment date are paid in full, and (b) Lender has received the notice required by this Article 13. Any partial prepayment permitted under Section 13.3 shall be applied to the outstanding principal balance in inverse order of maturity and shall not reduce or postpone any scheduled payment of principal or interest, and the regularly scheduled payments shall continue in effect.

**13.5 Involuntary Prepayments.** Any prepayment of the Loan resulting from the application of insurance proceeds or condemnation awards under Article 15, or from Lender's application of any reserve, escrow or other Collateral, shall be applied at par without any prepayment premium, penalty or yield maintenance amount.

**13.6 Acceleration Following an Event of Default.** The acceleration of the maturity of the Loan following an Event of Default is not a voluntary prepayment; however, the Yield Maintenance Premium that would have been payable under Section 13.2 had Borrower prepaid the Loan in full on the date of acceleration shall be due and payable as part of the Secured Obligations, together with interest at the Default Rate and all other amounts owing under the Loan Documents.

**13.7 No Other Prepayments.** Except as expressly provided in this Article 13 and in Article 15, Borrower shall not prepay the Loan in whole or in part, and no prepayment shall be made from the proceeds of any subordinate financing.

# ARTICLE 14 — EVENTS OF DEFAULT AND REMEDIES

**14.1 Events of Default.** Each of the following shall constitute an Event of Default under this Mortgage and the other Loan Documents:

(a) the failure of Borrower to pay any principal, interest, late charge, prepayment premium or any other amount due under the Loan Documents on or before the date when due, subject to the cure period in Section 14.2(a);

(b) the breach by Borrower of any covenant, agreement or obligation contained in this Mortgage or any other Loan Document, subject to the cure periods in Section 14.2;

(c) any representation or warranty made by Borrower or Guarantor in this Mortgage, any other Loan Document, or in any certificate, report or other document furnished in connection with the Loan, proves to have been false, misleading or inaccurate in any material respect when made or deemed made;

(d) the filing by or against Borrower or Guarantor of any petition under the United States Bankruptcy Code or any other insolvency, receivership, reorganization, arrangement, liquidation or similar proceeding, or the appointment of a receiver, trustee, custodian, sequestrator or similar official for Borrower, Guarantor or any substantial part of the property or assets of either, or any assignment for the benefit of creditors by Borrower or Guarantor, or any admission by Borrower or Guarantor of its inability to pay its debts generally as they become due, or any action by Borrower or Guarantor to authorize any of the foregoing;

(e) a default by Borrower or Guarantor under any other indebtedness for borrowed money in an amount exceeding Two Hundred Fifty Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($250,000.00), individually or in the aggregate, which default is not cured within any applicable cure or grace period;

(f) the failure of Borrower to maintain any insurance required by Article 9, subject to the cure period in Section 14.2(d);

(g) any violation of the transfer restrictions set forth in Section 7.3;

(h) the failure of Borrower to achieve Substantial Completion of the Renovation on or before the Substantial Completion Deadline;

(i) the DSCR falling below 1.25 to 1.00 for two (2) consecutive calendar quarters following the commencement of DSCR testing under Section 12.1, without cure in accordance with Section 12.6;

(j) any breach of the single-purpose entity or separateness covenants set forth in Section 6.12 or Section 7.6, or any amendment, modification or waiver of any single-purpose entity provision of Borrower's organizational documents in violation of Section 7.6;

(k) a material adverse change in the financial condition, business, assets or operations of Borrower or Guarantor that, in Lender's reasonable judgment, materially impairs the ability of Borrower to perform its obligations under the Loan Documents or of Guarantor to perform its obligations under the Guaranty;

(l) the failure of Borrower to comply with Article 11, or the modification, amendment, termination, release or violation of the LUR, or the receipt by Borrower or Lender of any notice from SCDHEC that SCDHEC Site ID SC-29403-0772 has been or may be reopened, or that the LUR has been or may be violated, modified or terminated;

(m) the occurrence of any default or event of default under any other Loan Document (including the Guaranty, the Completion Guaranty, the Interest Shortfall Guaranty and the Environmental Indemnity Agreement), after the expiration of any applicable cure period thereunder; or

(n) the occurrence of any other event or condition that constitutes an Event of Default under any other Loan Document.

**14.2 Cure Periods.** The following cure periods shall apply to the Events of Default described in Section 14.1:

(a) **Payment Defaults.** Five (5) Business Days after the date on which payment was due. The accrual of late charges under Section 2.6 and of interest at the Default Rate shall not be affected by the existence of this cure period.

(b) **Non-Monetary Defaults.** Thirty (30) calendar days after written notice from Lender to Borrower of the default; provided that if the default is of a nature that it cannot reasonably be cured within thirty (30) calendar days and Borrower has commenced and is diligently pursuing the cure, the cure period shall be extended for an additional period not to exceed sixty (60) calendar days (for a total cure period not to exceed ninety (90) calendar days), and provided further that no such extension shall apply if the failure to cure would reasonably be expected to result in the loss, forfeiture or material impairment of the Collateral or of Lender's lien or priority.

(c) **Single-Purpose Entity and Transfer Defaults.** No cure period. Any breach of Section 6.12, Section 7.3 or Section 7.6 shall constitute an immediate Event of Default without notice or opportunity to cure.

(d) **Insurance Defaults.** Ten (10) days after written notice from Lender to Borrower.

(e) **Land Use Restriction Defaults.** Ten (10) Business Days after written notice from Lender to Borrower, unless (i) SCDHEC has issued a notice of violation, order or directive with respect to the LUR, or (ii) the violation is not capable of being cured, in which case the Event of Default shall be immediate.

**14.3 Remedies Upon Default.** Upon the occurrence and during the continuance of an Event of Default, Lender may, in addition to all other rights and remedies available at law or in equity, exercise any one or more of the following remedies, cumulatively and without notice or demand (all of which are hereby waived to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law):

(a) declare the entire outstanding principal balance of the Loan, together with all accrued and unpaid interest and all other Secured Obligations, immediately due and payable, whereupon the same shall become immediately due and payable without presentment, demand, protest or further notice of any kind;

(b) enforce this Mortgage and foreclose the lien hereof in accordance with Section 14.4;

(c) exercise all rights and remedies with respect to the Leases and Rents under Article 4, and apply for the appointment of a receiver under Section 14.5;

(d) exercise all rights and remedies of a secured party under the UCC, including the right to take possession of the Collateral, to require Borrower to assemble the Collateral and make it available to Lender at a place designated by Lender, and to sell, lease or otherwise dispose of the Collateral, at public or private sale, with or without notice (Borrower acknowledging that ten (10) days' notice of any such sale is commercially reasonable);

(e) enter upon and take possession of the Property, and manage, operate, maintain, repair, renovate and lease the same, and collect the Rents;

(f) exercise all rights of Borrower under the GC Contract, the Plans, the Leases, the permits and the warranties, and complete or cause the completion of the Renovation;

(g) apply any or all reserves, escrows and other Collateral (including insurance proceeds and condemnation awards) to the Secured Obligations;

(h) recover judgment against Borrower for the Secured Obligations, to the extent provided in Section 16.2, and enforce any judgment against the Collateral;

(i) exercise its rights under the Guaranty, the Completion Guaranty, the Interest Shortfall Guaranty and the Environmental Indemnity Agreement; and

(j) exercise any other right or remedy available under the Loan Documents or applicable law.

**14.4 Judicial Foreclosure; No Power of Sale.** Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, Lender may foreclose this Mortgage in accordance with the laws of the State of South Carolina by an action in the Court of Common Pleas for Charleston County, South Carolina (or in any other court of competent jurisdiction), for the foreclosure and sale of the Property and the other Collateral, or for the enforcement of any of Lender's rights hereunder. Borrower acknowledges that the State of South Carolina is a judicial foreclosure jurisdiction and that this Mortgage does not, and shall not be construed to, grant Lender any power of sale exercisable without judicial proceedings. In any foreclosure action, Lender shall be entitled to a judgment for the Secured Obligations, for the sale of the Property and the other Collateral, for the appointment of a receiver, for its costs and expenses (including reasonable attorneys' fees and costs of title), and for a deficiency judgment to the extent permitted by applicable law. Borrower waives, to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, any right to require Lender to marshal assets or to pursue any particular remedy or any particular portion of the Collateral before pursuing any other remedy or portion. Nothing in this Section 14.4 or elsewhere in this Mortgage shall constitute a waiver of any right of redemption or statutory appraisal right that may not be waived under applicable law, and Lender's rights in respect of any deficiency shall be subject to Borrower's statutory appraisal rights under the laws of the State of South Carolina.

**14.5 Receiver.** Upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, Lender shall be entitled, as a matter of right and without notice to Borrower or any other Person and without regard to the adequacy of the security for the Secured Obligations, to the appointment of a receiver of the Property and the Rents (including rents accrued and unpaid and rents thereafter accruing) in any action to enforce this Mortgage or in any other proceeding. Any receiver so appointed shall have all powers necessary to manage, operate, maintain, repair, lease and otherwise deal with the Property, including the power to collect the Rents directly from tenants, and Borrower irrevocably consents to such appointment. The appointment of a receiver shall not impair or affect Lender's right to pursue foreclosure or any other remedy.

**14.6 Power of Attorney.** Borrower hereby irrevocably appoints Lender, effective upon the occurrence of an Event of Default, as its attorney-in-fact, with full power of substitution, to (a) notify tenants and collect the Rents, (b) complete the Renovation and deal with the General Contractor, subcontractors, architects and governmental authorities, (c) execute and deliver leases, amendments, notices, receipts, releases, lien waivers and other instruments with respect to the Property, (d) take any action required to comply with or cure any violation of the LUR or any Environmental Law, and (e) take any other action Lender deems necessary or appropriate to protect the Collateral and the Secured Obligations. This appointment is coupled with an interest and is irrevocable.

**14.7 Application of Proceeds.** All amounts received by Lender upon any sale or other disposition of the Collateral, and all Rents and other amounts received following an Event of Default, shall be applied in the following order: first, to the payment of all costs and expenses of the sale or enforcement, including reasonable attorneys' fees, court costs and title charges; second, to the payment of any protective advances made by Lender; third, to accrued and unpaid interest (including interest at the Default Rate), late charges and premiums; fourth, to the outstanding principal balance of the Loan; and fifth, to any other Secured Obligations, with any surplus paid to Borrower or to whomsoever may be lawfully entitled thereto, subject to applicable law.

**14.8 Deficiency.** If the proceeds of any foreclosure sale or other disposition of the Collateral are insufficient to pay the Secured Obligations in full, Borrower shall be liable for the deficiency only to the extent provided in Section 16.2, and Lender shall be entitled to a deficiency judgment to the extent permitted by applicable law, subject to Borrower's statutory appraisal rights.

**14.9 No Waiver; No Notice.** No failure or delay by Lender in exercising any right, power or remedy shall operate as a waiver thereof, and no single or partial exercise of any right, power or remedy shall preclude any other or further exercise thereof. Lender may exercise any remedy without prior notice or demand except as expressly required by this Mortgage or by applicable law, and Borrower waives presentment, demand for payment, protest, notice of dishonor, notice of nonpayment, notice of acceleration and notice of intent to accelerate, to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law.

**14.10 Lender's Right to Perform.** If Borrower fails to perform any obligation under this Mortgage, Lender may (but shall not be obligated to) perform such obligation, and any amounts expended by Lender shall be Secured Obligations bearing interest at the Default Rate, payable on demand and secured by this Mortgage, and shall not constitute a waiver of the underlying Event of Default.

**14.11 Remedies Cumulative.** No remedy conferred upon Lender is intended to be exclusive of any other remedy, and each and every remedy shall be cumulative and in addition to every other remedy given hereunder, now or hereafter existing at law, in equity, by statute or otherwise.

**14.12 Waiver of Certain Defenses.** To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Borrower waives (a) any defense based on the statute of limitations, (b) any defense based on the doctrine of election of remedies, (c) any right to assert against Lender any claim, defense or setoff that Borrower may have against any other Person, and (d) any right to require Lender to proceed against any other Person or any other collateral. Nothing in this Section 14.12 shall limit any defense or right that may not be waived under applicable law.

# ARTICLE 15 — CASUALTY AND CONDEMNATION

**15.1 Notice.** Borrower shall give Lender prompt written notice of any fire or other casualty affecting the Property and of any actual or threatened condemnation, eminent domain proceeding, taking or conveyance in lieu thereof affecting the Property or any portion thereof or any easement or right-of-way therein.

**15.2 Casualty.** Upon any casualty, Borrower shall promptly commence and diligently pursue the adjustment of the insurance claim and, subject to this Section 15.2, the restoration of the Property. Lender shall have the right to participate in the adjustment of any claim in excess of Two Hundred Fifty Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($250,000.00). If the casualty loss is less than Five Hundred Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($500,000.00), no Event of Default exists, and the insurance proceeds are sufficient to complete the restoration, Borrower may apply the proceeds to the restoration of the Property in accordance with plans approved by Lender. If the casualty loss equals or exceeds Five Hundred Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($500,000.00), or if an Event of Default exists, or if the proceeds are insufficient to complete the restoration, or if the restoration cannot reasonably be completed within twelve (12) months after the casualty, Lender may elect, in its sole discretion, either (a) to permit Borrower to restore the Property subject to such conditions as Lender may reasonably impose, including the deposit of the proceeds into a Lender-controlled escrow account and the satisfaction of the conditions set forth in Section 15.4, or (b) to apply the insurance proceeds to the Secured Obligations in accordance with Section 15.5.

**15.3 Condemnation.** Upon any taking or threatened taking, Lender may elect, in its sole discretion, either (a) to permit Borrower to restore the remaining Property (to the extent restoration is reasonably practicable) and to apply the condemnation award to such restoration subject to the conditions in Section 15.4, or (b) to apply the condemnation award to the Secured Obligations in accordance with Section 15.5. Borrower shall not settle, compromise or agree to any award without Lender's prior written consent if the award exceeds Two Hundred Fifty Thousand and No/100 Dollars ($250,000.00).

**15.4 Conditions to Restoration.** As a condition to any restoration with insurance proceeds or condemnation awards, (a) no Event of Default shall exist; (b) the restoration shall be completed in accordance with plans approved by Lender, in compliance with all Applicable Laws and in a workmanlike manner, and shall restore the Property to a condition at least equal to its condition immediately prior to the casualty or taking; (c) the proceeds, together with any additional amounts deposited by Borrower, shall be sufficient to complete the restoration; (d) if the restoration involves any work affecting the ground-floor slab of Bay 1 on Lot 7, the requirements of Sections 8.13 and 11.3 shall be satisfied; and (e) Borrower shall have delivered to Lender such architect's certificates, contracts, lien waivers and title date-down endorsements as Lender may reasonably require. All proceeds held by Lender for restoration shall be disbursed in accordance with Article 8, with appropriate adjustments to reflect the scope of the restoration work.

**15.5 Application of Proceeds to the Secured Obligations.** Any insurance proceeds or condemnation awards that Lender elects to apply to the Secured Obligations shall be applied at par, without any prepayment premium, penalty or yield maintenance amount, in the order set forth in Section 14.7, and shall be applied first to accrued interest, then to principal, and shall not postpone or reduce any scheduled payment.

**15.6 Failure to Restore.** If Borrower fails to commence and diligently pursue any restoration to which Lender has consented, or fails to complete such restoration within the period approved by Lender, Lender may undertake or complete the restoration, and all amounts expended by Lender, together with interest at the Default Rate, shall be Secured Obligations.

# ARTICLE 16 — GUARANTOR; NON-RECOURSE; LIMITATION OF LIABILITY

**16.1 Guaranty.** The obligations of Borrower under this Mortgage and the other Loan Documents are guaranteed by Guarantor pursuant to the Guaranty (including the non-recourse carve-out guaranty), the Completion Guaranty and the Interest Shortfall Guaranty, and are further supported by the Environmental Indemnity Agreement. Lender may proceed against Guarantor under the Guaranty without first proceeding against Borrower, the Property or any other Collateral, and without any obligation to exhaust any remedy.

**16.2 Limitation of Liability; Non-Recourse.** Except as provided in Section 16.3 and in the Environmental Indemnity Agreement, Lender shall look solely to the Collateral for the payment of the Secured Obligations, and no Member of Borrower, and no manager, officer, employee or Affiliate of Borrower or of any Member, shall have any personal liability for the payment or performance of the Secured Obligations. Nothing in this Section 16.2 shall (a) limit the liability of Guarantor under the Guaranty, the Completion Guaranty, the Interest Shortfall Guaranty or the Environmental Indemnity Agreement, (b) constitute a release of Borrower from any obligation under the Loan Documents, (c) limit the liability of any Person for its own fraud, misrepresentation or willful misconduct, or (d) limit Lender's right to collect the Secured Obligations from the Collateral and from any Person that has expressly assumed the obligations of Borrower in writing.

**16.3 Recourse Carve-Outs.** Notwithstanding Section 16.2, Guarantor shall be fully and personally liable for the entire outstanding amount of the Secured Obligations (and Borrower shall be liable for the entire amount of the Secured Obligations to the extent provided in the Guaranty) upon the occurrence of any of the following (collectively, the "**Carve-Out Events**"), whether or not caused by or within the control of Borrower or Guarantor:

(a) fraud, intentional misrepresentation or willful misconduct by Borrower or Guarantor, or any of their respective agents, in connection with the Loan or the Property;

(b) misapplication or misappropriation of Rents, security deposits, insurance proceeds, condemnation awards or any reserve or escrow held by or on behalf of Lender;

(c) the voluntary filing of a petition in bankruptcy or any other insolvency proceeding by or on behalf of Borrower, or Borrower's consent to the appointment of a receiver or to the entry of an order for relief in any involuntary proceeding, or Borrower's cooperation with any Person in causing any such filing, consent or order;

(d) environmental liability arising from or relating to the acts or omissions of Borrower, Guarantor or their respective agents with respect to Hazardous Materials at the Property, and any violation of the LUR, in each case to the extent provided in the Environmental Indemnity Agreement and this Article 16;

(e) any violation of the transfer restrictions set forth in Section 7.3;

(f) the failure of Borrower to obtain or maintain insurance required by Article 9 following Lender's written notice and the expiration of the cure period in Section 14.2(d), to the extent of any loss not covered as a result thereof;

(g) the failure of Borrower to comply with Section 7.2 or Section 7.3 resulting in the creation of a lien or encumbrance senior to or pari passu with this Mortgage;

(h) the failure of Borrower to comply with the single-purpose entity and separateness covenants in Section 6.12 or Section 7.6, if such failure results in the substantive consolidation of Borrower with any other Person in any bankruptcy or insolvency proceeding;

(i) Borrower's assertion in any proceeding that any Loan Document is not a valid, binding and enforceable obligation of Borrower; or

(j) Borrower's failure to complete the Renovation in accordance with Article 8, to the extent provided in the Completion Guaranty.

**16.4 Environmental Indemnity Not Limited.** The obligations of Borrower and Guarantor under the Environmental Indemnity Agreement and Article 11 are full recourse obligations and are not limited or affected by Section 16.2, by the value or sufficiency of the Collateral, by any foreclosure, or by the release of this Mortgage.

**16.5 Guarantor Acknowledgments.** Guarantor has executed this Mortgage solely for purposes of acknowledging the provisions of this Article 16 and the provisions of Article 11, and such acknowledgment shall not be construed as imposing on Guarantor any obligation other than those set forth in the Guaranty, the Completion Guaranty, the Interest Shortfall Guaranty and the Environmental Indemnity Agreement.

**16.6 Interest Shortfall Guaranty.** Without limiting the foregoing, the Interest Shortfall Guaranty guarantees payment of any shortfall in monthly interest payments due under the Note during the first fourteen (14) months following the Closing Date (through and including June 15, 2026), to the extent that Net Operating Income from the Property is insufficient to cover such monthly interest payments, all as more particularly provided in the Interest Shortfall Guaranty. Borrower acknowledges that the Interest Shortfall Guaranty does not reduce, waive or defer any payment obligation of Borrower under the Note or this Mortgage, and that all payments of interest and principal remain due in accordance with the Note.

# ARTICLE 17 — MISCELLANEOUS

**17.1 Amendments; Waivers.** This Mortgage may be amended, modified or supplemented only by a written instrument signed by Borrower and Lender. No waiver of any provision of this Mortgage, or of any breach or default, shall be effective unless in writing signed by Lender, and no such waiver shall be deemed a waiver of any other provision, breach or default or of any subsequent breach or default. Lender's acceptance of any payment after the due date shall not constitute a waiver of the Event of Default arising therefrom.

**17.2 Severability.** If any provision of this Mortgage is held to be invalid, illegal or unenforceable in any respect, such invalidity, illegality or unenforceability shall not affect any other provision, and this Mortgage shall be construed as if such provision had never been contained herein, to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law.

**17.3 Entire Agreement; Conflict.** The Loan Documents constitute the entire agreement of the parties with respect to the Loan and supersede all prior agreements and understandings. In the event of any conflict between the terms of the Term Sheet and the terms of this Mortgage or any other Loan Document, the terms of this Mortgage or such other Loan Document shall control. In the event of any conflict between this Mortgage and the Note with respect to the payment of principal, interest or prepayment premiums, the Note shall control.

**17.4 Successors and Assigns.** This Mortgage shall bind and benefit Borrower and Lender and their respective successors and permitted assigns. Borrower may not assign, delegate or transfer any of its rights or obligations under this Mortgage without Lender's prior written consent, and any attempted assignment without such consent shall be void. Lender may assign, sell, participate or otherwise transfer all or any portion of its interest in the Loan and this Mortgage (including to any Federal Home Loan Bank or in connection with any securitization) without Borrower's consent, and in connection therewith may disclose to any actual or prospective assignee, participant, rating agency or investor all information relating to Borrower, Guarantor and the Property, subject to customary confidentiality arrangements.

**17.5 No Third-Party Beneficiaries.** Except for Lender's successors and assigns and the indemnified parties under the Environmental Indemnity Agreement and Section 17.10, nothing in this Mortgage shall confer any right or remedy upon any Person other than the parties hereto.

**17.6 Notices.** All notices, demands, consents, approvals and other communications under this Mortgage shall be in writing and shall be deemed duly given (a) when delivered personally, (b) one Business Day after deposit with a nationally recognized overnight courier, or (c) three (3) Business Days after deposit in the United States mail, certified or registered, postage prepaid, return receipt requested, addressed as follows (or to such other address as a party may designate by notice given in accordance with this Section 17.6):

