**17.17 Lender's Discretion.** Whenever this Mortgage provides that Lender may act in its discretion, or that a matter must be satisfactory to Lender, such determination shall be made by Lender in good faith and in accordance with commercially reasonable standards, unless this Mortgage expressly provides that Lender may act in its sole discretion, in which case Lender's discretion shall be absolute, subject only to the implied covenant of good faith and fair dealing.

**17.18 Business Day Convention.** If any Payment Date or other date on which performance is required is not a Business Day, such date shall be extended to the next succeeding Business Day, and interest shall continue to accrue during such extension.

**17.19 Copies; Lost Instruments.** Borrower shall be entitled to a copy (which may be electronic) of this Mortgage and the other Loan Documents as executed. No lost instrument affidavit shall be required as a condition to any enforcement action in which Lender produces a copy of the recorded Mortgage.

